0% within 2 years (weather prediction false positive rates remain 15-30%)\n- **Mitigation:** Confidence intervals in all predictions, human oversight required for high-stakes decisions\n\n**3. Infrastructure Vulnerability**\n- **Scenario:** Major climate event damages regional hubs, causing cascading failures\n- **Probability:** 80% within 10 years\n- **Mitigation:** Distributed architecture, mobile backup systems, rapid deployment capabilities\n\n### 🟡 **HIGH PROBABILITY, MEDIUM IMPACT RISKS**\n\n**4. Talent Acquisition Failure**\n- **Scenario:** Cannot hire 100+ specialized staff across diverse regions with required skills\n- **Probability:** 65%\n- **Mitigation:** Partnership with universities for talent pipeline, remote work options, competitive compensation\n\n**5. Regulatory Obstacles**\n- **Scenario:** Data privacy laws, spectrum regulations, or export controls block deployment\n- **Probability:** 80%\n- **Mitigation:** Early legal engagement, compliance-by-design, regulatory sandbox participation\n\n## COHERENCE EVALUATION\n\n### ❌ **CRITICAL INCOHERENCES**\n\n**1. Autonomy vs Human Oversight Paradox**\n- **Issue:** Plan calls for 70% autonomous decisions by Year 5 while simultaneously emphasizing community control\n- **Reality Check:** Community-driven systems cannot be 70% autonomous without losing community control\n- **Resolution:** Clarify decision boundaries - technical optimization autonomous, community impact decisions require human approval\n\n**2. Revenue vs Mission Conflict**\n- **Issue:** Plan assumes commercial revenue generation while positioning as public good\n- **Reality Check:** Data monetization creates incentives that may conflict with equitable access\n- **Resolution:** Establish trust/NGO structure with clear conflict-of-interest policies\n\n**3. Speed vs Quality Trade-off**\n- **Issue:** 72-month timeline demands shortcuts that compromise system robustness\n- **Reality Check:** Critical infrastructure (GPS, internet) took 15-20 years to achieve global reliability\n- **Resolution:** Extend timeline to 10-15 years with clear phase gates\n\n### ✅ **COHERENT ELEMENTS**\n\n**1. Technical Architecture:** Well-designed layered approach with appropriate technology choices\n**2. Risk Management:** Comprehensive risk identification and mitigation strategies\n**3. Community-Centered Design:** Strong emphasis on local engagement and cultural sensitivity\n\n## STRATEGIC PIVOT RECOMMENDATIONS\n\n### **IMMEDIATE PIVOT (Next 90 Days)**\n\n**1. Reduce Scope to Single-Hazard Pilot**\n```\nCHANGE FROM: Multi-hazard global network\nCHANGE TO: Flood prediction system in 2 pilot regions (Bangladesh + Netherlands)\n```\n\n**2. Secure Proof-of-Concept Funding**\n```\nTARGET: $5M over 18 months (down from $50M in 9 months)\nFUNDING SOURCES: \n- 2 national governments ($2M each)\n- 1 philanthropic foundation ($1M)\n```\n\n**3. Establish Technical Proof**\n```\nDEMONSTRATE: 500 IoT sensors + satellite data integration\nMETRIC: 85% accuracy for 7-day flood predictions in pilot regions\n```\n\n**4. Community Partnership Validation**\n```\nPARTNER: 1 local NGO with 10+ year track record in each pilot region\nPROCESS: Co-design workshops with 100+ community members\nOUTPUT: Community-approved system requirements\n```\n\n### **STRATEGIC REFRAME (Next 6-12 Months)**\n\n**1. Position as \"Climate Data Cooperative\"**\n- **Instead of:** Top-down global network\n- **Position as:** Federated system owned/operated by participating communities and governments\n\n**2. Focus on \"Minimum Viable Early Warning\"**\n- **Instead of:** Comprehensive resilience platform\n- **Focus on:** High-accuracy, long-lead-time alerts for one hazard type\n\n**3. Build on Existing Infrastructure**\n- **Instead of:** Building from scratch\n- **Strategy:** Integrate with WHO early warning systems, WMO networks, national weather services\n\n### **DECISIVE NEXT STEPS (Priority Order)**\n\n**PRIORITY 1 (Month 1): Community Assessment**\n- **Action:** Deploy co